=== FIX COMMIT 609c44c55 ===
KS-1004: an anchor time is carried only alongside a hash; the guard cell that pinned the retired txHash arm is re-stated as the union

Round-2 fix on top of the develop merge. Three files, nothing else.

anchorStateSync.ts — ONE line of product: the anchoredAt carry narrows from
`prior?.anchoredAt` to `prior?.txHash && prior?.anchoredAt`. An anchor time is
retained only for a transaction that was built and then failed; a no-hash
fail-closed blob has none, which is what the blob type's own comment
(documentRepo.ts:60-61) says. The reviewer's item 2 is answered by the code
staying inside the comment's contract rather than by editing the comment (that
file is another open PR's). txHash / blockHeight / network carries unchanged.

ks1058-anchor-failed-preserves-thread-token.test.ts — the last cell, "CONTROL:
the existing guard still no-ops on a document carrying a real txHash", pinned
the very arm this branch retires and went red BY DESIGN on the merged tree
(measured at the merge commit 323151415: 4 of 6, the CONTRACT anchoredAt cell
and this one). It is re-stated as the union of both tickets: the same hashed
prior IS written, status anchor_failed, txHash and blockHeight carried,
threadToken preserved. The other five cells are untouched; the CONTRACT cell
goes green on the narrowed carry. File header untouched.

ks1004-anchor-failed-lockout.test.ts — one new cell (9 now): a NO-txHash prior
carrying anchoredAt does not keep it. The CONTRACT from this side of the fence.

